# Local runs only (`pnpm dev`, and the preview the end-to-end tests run against): wrangler never uploads this file, so
# no deployment has what stands here. NO SECRET may ever be written into it.
#
# DAILY_WALLS is the day's budget of walls (wrangler.jsonc sets it for the deployment). Local runs keep their storage between runs, and a day
# of end-to-end tests makes more walls than that: without a number of their own, the tests of the afternoon would be
# refused their walls. The Worker's own tests do not read this file's number: they name theirs in vitest.config.ts.
DAILY_WALLS=1000000
# The AI's budget in neurons for any 24 hours (wrangler.jsonc sets it for the deployment): the stand-in below reckons
# what a run would have cost and books it, and a day of end-to-end tests arranges more often than 8,000 neurons allow.
DAILY_NEURONS=1000000
# Local runs never ask Cloudflare's AI: with this switch the route `POST /api/walls/:id/arrange` asks a stand-in that
# needs no network and no login and answers the same every time: it puts the notes together that begin with the same
# word (packages/arrange/src/fake.ts). A deployment does not have this variable and asks the binding `AI`.
ARRANGE_FAKE=1
